# guard-positive-controls.manifest — every guard that declares a population
# (`guard-populations.manifest`) and the POSITIVE CONTROL it ships with: the
# assertion in which a PLANTED violation is demonstrably caught, or a planted
# malformed input demonstrably REFUSED. Recorded as DATA rather than prose,
# because prose cannot be made to fail.
#
# Enforced by:  bash monitor/watcher/test-guard-positive-controls.sh
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (your-org/nexus-code#1264 R4, #1477) ──────────────
#
# "Every guard must ship with a planted violation it demonstrably catches, and
# go red if that plant stops being caught." The case that made it a rule:
# `test-assert-shims-wrapped.sh` was GREEN for the whole of an 18-hour outage
# CAUSED BY THE GUARD IT TESTS (#1477) — its hermetic seam could not observe the
# guard's own failure class. A guard never seen to fail is not evidence; a
# suite whose plants are all inside a seam proves only the seam.
#
# ── THE SWEEP IS THE POINT (#1264's binding finding) ───────────────────────
#
# A rule adopted without an enumeration of its current violators reproduces
# the defect #1264 diagnoses (c386bff added a rule, its test, and left the
# documented violation in the pre-push gate for 14 days). So this file is the
# sweep: one row per declaring guard, ALL of them, and the guards with NO
# positive control are named as `NONE` rows with a reason and bounded by the
# `none-ceiling` below — a ratchet, never a running total. Census taken at
# dev 2a299572, 2026-09-06, by reading each suite's assertion labels for a
# planted violation the guard is asserted to catch.
#
# ── NO NAME-DERIVATION (the #1121 shape) ───────────────────────────────────
#
# A grep over each suite for "control|plant|potency" is a HEURISTIC — it
# under-finds (five suites spell their plant `fixture:`, `the pre-fix red`,
# `positive.sh:3:`) and over-finds (`Control A: extracted exactly N forms` is a
# GENERATOR check, not a plant). So the control is DECLARED per row, as a
# verbatim substring of the assertion label in the owner suite; the only
# generated thing is the guard set the rows are checked against.
#
# ── WHAT A ROW CLAIMS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT ─────────────────────────────────
#
# Structural: the guard exists and is tracked, and the named label appears
# verbatim in it — so a renamed or deleted plant reddens here. Whether the
# plant is actually CAUGHT is the owner suite's own assertion, which this
# ratchet does not re-run; a `plant` row whose owner stops asserting red on
# its plant is a defect in the OWNER (its label would change) and shows here
# only if the label text moves.
#
# ── COLUMNS  guard|control_label|kind|reason ────────────────────────────────
#
#   plant     a planted VIOLATION the guard is asserted to flag / detect / fire on
#   refusal   a planted MALFORMED input (empty path, unparseable file, missing
#             rows) the guard is asserted to REFUSE with a stated status —
#             the fail-closed direction, deliberately distinguished from a plant
#   none      no positive control found in the suite's assertion labels at the
#             census ref; bounded by the ceiling; the reason says what a plant
#             would have to look like AND carries an OWNER — a tracker ref
#             (`#NNN` / `owner/repo#NNN`) or an expiry (`until:YYYY-MM-DD`) —
#             so the exemption has to be re-justified rather than inherited
#             (your-org/nexus-code#1469: an unowned exemption invites a shrug,
#             and that one turned out to be unnecessary as well as unowned)
#
# none-ceiling: 0
#
